{"name":"Camerabot (Commercial)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>A favorite of celebrities, musicians, and streamers alike, this round floating minibot rotates around its user while recording or streaming audio or video. The user of this minibot can perform the Livestream exploration activity at the same time as another exploration activity. A camerabot only takes 1 charge per hour it remains active.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":0},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":100}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"camerabot-commercial","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"camerabot"}},"_id":"21c40c4ea15d364c"}
{"name":"Camerabot (Tactical)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>A favorite of celebrities, musicians, and streamers alike, this round floating minibot rotates around its user while recording or streaming audio or video. The user of this minibot can perform the Livestream exploration activity at the same time as another exploration activity. A camerabot only takes 1 charge per hour it remains active.</p>\n<p>A tactical camerabot has a built-in flashlight and can be directed to record others, including specific creatures or locations. It must remain within 100 feet of its owner, or it immediately attempts to recall itself back to its owner.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":2},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":250}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"camerabot-tactical","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"camerabot"}},"_id":"fd8ed7f67b271d7d"}
{"name":"Camerabot (Advanced)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>A favorite of celebrities, musicians, and streamers alike, this round floating minibot rotates around its user while recording or streaming audio or video. The user of this minibot can perform the Livestream exploration activity at the same time as another exploration activity. A camerabot only takes 1 charge per hour it remains active.</p>\n<p>A tactical camerabot has a built-in flashlight and can be directed to record others, including specific creatures or locations. It must remain within 100 feet of its owner, or it immediately attempts to recall itself back to its owner.</p><p>An advanced camerabot can record within 1,000 feet and has darkvision, allowing it to record without a light source.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":4},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":1000}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"camerabot-advanced","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"camerabot"}},"_id":"afb15a75b8f371de"}
{"name":"Medbot (Commercial)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Medbots can be found across the galaxy assisting first responders and nurses, standing by in public venues and sporting events, or even following medics on the battlefield. The medbot has an integrated medkit that can be used even when it isn’t activated (but it can’t be worn).</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":2},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":250}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"medbot-commercial","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"medbot"}},"_id":"c5f7d2914cd25fd6"}
{"name":"Medbot (Tactical)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Medbots can be found across the galaxy assisting first responders and nurses, standing by in public venues and sporting events, or even following medics on the battlefield. The medbot has an integrated medkit that can be used even when it isn’t activated (but it can’t be worn).</p>\n<p>The tactical medbot has an integrated tactical medkit.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":4},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":700}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"medbot-tactical","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"medbot"}},"_id":"61d31ef25711aa03"}
{"name":"Petbot","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Petbots resemble specific Tiny animals, despite clearly being robots. It’s possible to hide an object of light Bulk in a petbot, but it takes 1 minute to access the compartment. You gain a +1 item bonus to Stealth checks to Conceal an Object in a petbot.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":0},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":50}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"petbot","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"petbot"}},"_id":"6f1a732ad5e04a12"}
{"name":"Beatbot (Commercial)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Regularly seen accompanying vid streamers who like ambient music to make their livestreams more engaging on location, a beatbot consists of several parts. A floating “docking station” provides a charging pad for several small levitating speakers. The minibot uses these speakers to create a dynamic soundscape centered around the dock.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Drop the Beat</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span> (auditory, manipulate)</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You Command the minibot to play some music or generate a personal soundtrack tailored to whatever you’re doing, shifting reactively to your behavior and dialogue. You take a –4 penalty to Stealth checks while the music is playing. You can Dismiss this effect.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":1},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":100}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"beatbot-commercial","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"beatbot"}},"_id":"331de3bfb18beed8"}
{"name":"Beatbot (Tactical)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Regularly seen accompanying vid streamers who like ambient music to make their livestreams more engaging on location, a beatbot consists of several parts. A floating “docking station” provides a charging pad for several small levitating speakers. The minibot uses these speakers to create a dynamic soundscape centered around the dock.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Drop the Beat</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span> (auditory, manipulate)</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You Command the minibot to play some music or generate a personal soundtrack tailored to whatever you’re doing, shifting reactively to your behavior and dialogue. You take a –4 penalty to Stealth checks while the music is playing. You can Dismiss this effect.</p>\n<p>Drop the Beat provides a +1 item bonus to Performance checks. During your daily preparations, you can use 5 charges of the beatbot’s battery to set it to record 24 hours of audio that it can recall on command.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":3},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":500}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"beatbot-tactical","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"beatbot"}},"_id":"a19901ca05609816"}
{"name":"Bellbot (Commercial)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Bellbots are effectively suitcases with legs, wheels, or tracks that can follow their owners around workplaces and spaceports. They have basic danger avoidance protocols to avoid hazardous terrain and environments that could damage their payloads, though they can be commanded to ignore these protocols. A commercial bellbot has a Speed of 25 feet (but no fly Speed) and holds up to 4 Bulk of items, and the first 2 Bulk don’t apply to the Bulk of a bellbot.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Bellhop</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span></p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The bellbot follows you until deactivated. This lasts 1 hour and expends 1 battery charge.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":1},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":150}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"bellbot-commercial","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"bellbot"}},"_id":"7fc5fa5930b18833"}
{"name":"Bellbot (Tactical)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Bellbots are effectively suitcases with legs, wheels, or tracks that can follow their owners around workplaces and spaceports. They have basic danger avoidance protocols to avoid hazardous terrain and environments that could damage their payloads, though they can be commanded to ignore these protocols. A commercial bellbot has a Speed of 25 feet (but no fly Speed) and holds up to 4 Bulk of items, and the first 2 Bulk don’t apply to the Bulk of a bellbot.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Bellhop</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span></p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The bellbot follows you until deactivated. This lasts 1 hour and expends 1 battery charge.</p>\n<p>A tactical bellbot has a fly Speed of 30 feet and an integrated <em>commercial null space chamber</em>.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":5},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":1150}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"bellbot-tactical","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"bellbot"}},"_id":"7bf0dd9823965d27"}
{"name":"Bellbot (Advanced)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Bellbots are effectively suitcases with legs, wheels, or tracks that can follow their owners around workplaces and spaceports. They have basic danger avoidance protocols to avoid hazardous terrain and environments that could damage their payloads, though they can be commanded to ignore these protocols. A commercial bellbot has a Speed of 25 feet (but no fly Speed) and holds up to 4 Bulk of items, and the first 2 Bulk don’t apply to the Bulk of a bellbot.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Bellhop</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span></p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The bellbot follows you until deactivated. This lasts 1 hour and expends 1 battery charge.</p>\n<p>A tactical bellbot has a fly Speed of 30 feet and an integrated <em>commercial null space chamber</em>.</p><p>An advanced bellbot has a fly Speed of 30 feet and an integrated <em>tactical null space chamber</em>.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":8},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":4150}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"bellbot-advanced","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"bellbot"}},"_id":"9cb730a3911d7922"}
{"name":"Bellbot (Superior)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Bellbots are effectively suitcases with legs, wheels, or tracks that can follow their owners around workplaces and spaceports. They have basic danger avoidance protocols to avoid hazardous terrain and environments that could damage their payloads, though they can be commanded to ignore these protocols. A commercial bellbot has a Speed of 25 feet (but no fly Speed) and holds up to 4 Bulk of items, and the first 2 Bulk don’t apply to the Bulk of a bellbot.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Bellhop</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span></p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The bellbot follows you until deactivated. This lasts 1 hour and expends 1 battery charge.</p>\n<p>A tactical bellbot has a fly Speed of 30 feet and an integrated <em>commercial null space chamber</em>.</p><p>An advanced bellbot has a fly Speed of 30 feet and an integrated <em>tactical null space chamber</em>.</p><p>A superior bellbot has a fly Speed of 30 feet and an integrated <em>advanced null space chamber</em>.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":12},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":16150}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"bellbot-superior","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"bellbot"}},"_id":"c979918fd2f5ae91"}
{"name":"Bellbot (Elite)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Bellbots are effectively suitcases with legs, wheels, or tracks that can follow their owners around workplaces and spaceports. They have basic danger avoidance protocols to avoid hazardous terrain and environments that could damage their payloads, though they can be commanded to ignore these protocols. A commercial bellbot has a Speed of 25 feet (but no fly Speed) and holds up to 4 Bulk of items, and the first 2 Bulk don’t apply to the Bulk of a bellbot.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Bellhop</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span></p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The bellbot follows you until deactivated. This lasts 1 hour and expends 1 battery charge.</p>\n<p>A tactical bellbot has a fly Speed of 30 feet and an integrated <em>commercial null space chamber</em>.</p><p>An advanced bellbot has a fly Speed of 30 feet and an integrated <em>tactical null space chamber</em>.</p><p>A superior bellbot has a fly Speed of 30 feet and an integrated <em>advanced null space chamber</em>.</p><p>An elite bellbot has a fly Speed of 30 feet and an integrated <em>superior null space chamber</em>.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":14},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":36150}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"bellbot-elite","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"bellbot"}},"_id":"2e1deccb3f7acdcd"}
{"name":"Butlerbot (Commercial)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Butlerbots diligently follow their owner around and help with all those pesky little things like keeping your appearance top notch, reminding you to hydrate, and helping you find a missing access card if you can’t remember where you left it. Butlerbots are something of a status symbol among the elite and come in a variety of colors and materials, depending on how much one wants to spend.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Buttle</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span> (auditory, manipulate)</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You order your butlerbot to perform one of the following core functions.</p><p><strong>Clean</strong> Clean an object of light Bulk or less.</p><p><strong>Find</strong> Recall for you the location of an object. If the butlerbot doesn’t know where the object is, it can help you Seek the object, giving you a +1 item bonus to your Perception check to Search for the object.</p><p><strong>Remind</strong> The butlerbot gives any number of verbal reminders you’ve set during your daily preparations. If you set a reminder for a specific time, it reactivates to remind you at that time, up to 24 hours after you use this action.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":4},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":1000}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"butlerbot-commercial","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"butlerbot"}},"_id":"f491ca56c06e9a92"}
{"name":"Butlerbot (Tactical)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Butlerbots diligently follow their owner around and help with all those pesky little things like keeping your appearance top notch, reminding you to hydrate, and helping you find a missing access card if you can’t remember where you left it. Butlerbots are something of a status symbol among the elite and come in a variety of colors and materials, depending on how much one wants to spend.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Buttle</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span> (auditory, manipulate)</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You order your butlerbot to perform one of the following core functions.</p><p><strong>Clean</strong> Clean an object of light Bulk or less.</p><p><strong>Find</strong> Recall for you the location of an object. If the butlerbot doesn’t know where the object is, it can help you Seek the object, giving you a +1 item bonus to your Perception check to Search for the object.</p><p><strong>Remind</strong> The butlerbot gives any number of verbal reminders you’ve set during your daily preparations. If you set a reminder for a specific time, it reactivates to remind you at that time, up to 24 hours after you use this action.</p>\n<p>A tactical butlerbot is crafted by an artisan with exquisite material and uses 5 charges of its battery each day to constantly scan local infospheres for friendly reminders it takes the liberty of transmitting (verbally or directly to your comm unit) when you’re about to commit a social faux pas, including forgetting someone’s name or telling an inappropriate joke. This grants you a +1 item bonus to Diplomacy checks to Make an Impression and to Society checks to Recall Knowledge about important personalities, societal structures, and local etiquette.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":10},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":10000}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"butlerbot-tactical","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"butlerbot"}},"_id":"4e0c4ac5bd5541e8"}
{"name":"Firebot (Commercial)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>The modern era doesn't reduce the risk of being set on fire, and with laser fire happening more often in certain kinds of professions, firebots help with maintaining safety. A firebot uses an integrated commercial fire extinguisher and can hold twice as much chem as any fire extinguisher it has installed. A firebot has resistance 12 to fire damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Extinguish</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span></p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You order the firebot to Fly and use its integrated fire extinguisher.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":4},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":1050}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"firebot-commercial","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"firebot"}},"_id":"7055106552198c26"}
{"name":"Firebot (Tactical)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>The modern era doesn't reduce the risk of being set on fire, and with laser fire happening more often in certain kinds of professions, firebots help with maintaining safety. A firebot uses an integrated commercial fire extinguisher and can hold twice as much chem as any fire extinguisher it has installed. A firebot has resistance 12 to fire damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Extinguish</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span></p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You order the firebot to Fly and use its integrated fire extinguisher.</p>\n<p>The fire resistance is 24, and the fire extinguisher is tactical.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":9},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":5750}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"firebot-tactical","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"firebot"}},"_id":"ed9e70a3413b56ed"}
{"name":"Firebot (Advanced)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>The modern era doesn't reduce the risk of being set on fire, and with laser fire happening more often in certain kinds of professions, firebots help with maintaining safety. A firebot uses an integrated commercial fire extinguisher and can hold twice as much chem as any fire extinguisher it has installed. A firebot has resistance 12 to fire damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Extinguish</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span></p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You order the firebot to Fly and use its integrated fire extinguisher.</p>\n<p>The fire resistance is 24, and the fire extinguisher is tactical.</p><p>The fire resistance is 36, and the fire extinguisher is advanced.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":14},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":36050}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"firebot-advanced","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"firebot"}},"_id":"588a3ce593d2af8a"}
{"name":"Glampbot (Commercial)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>The glampbot, a must-have for outdoor influencers, makes camping in the wilderness as comfortable and effortless as possible. Its primary function is to safely guide you back to civilization. Other glampbots can assemble a tent, start small fires, calculate weather forecasts, and even synthesize food using UPBs. Glampbots use solar panels to recharge their internal batteries, allowing them to stay active as long as they get at least 6 hours of sunlight for every 24 hours they remain activated.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Glamp On!</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span> (auditory, manipulate)</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You command the glampbot to guide you back to a specific location. If you’re on a planet without GPS satellites, it can only return you to locations the glampbot has physically been before.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":1},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":100}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"glampbot-commercial","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"glampbot"}},"_id":"a0baea9fe25b3937"}
{"name":"Glampbot (Tactical)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>The glampbot, a must-have for outdoor influencers, makes camping in the wilderness as comfortable and effortless as possible. Its primary function is to safely guide you back to civilization. Other glampbots can assemble a tent, start small fires, calculate weather forecasts, and even synthesize food using UPBs. Glampbots use solar panels to recharge their internal batteries, allowing them to stay active as long as they get at least 6 hours of sunlight for every 24 hours they remain activated.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Glamp On!</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span> (auditory, manipulate)</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You command the glampbot to guide you back to a specific location. If you’re on a planet without GPS satellites, it can only return you to locations the glampbot has physically been before.</p>\n<p>A tactical glampbot can help build a camp, providing a +1 item bonus to Survival checks to Subsist when building a shelter. It can also synthesize an edible meal with enough sustenance for a creature for 1 day by using 1 UPB.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":3},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":450}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"glampbot-tactical","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"glampbot"}},"_id":"ae22e7db70866938"}
{"name":"Glampbot (Advanced)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>The glampbot, a must-have for outdoor influencers, makes camping in the wilderness as comfortable and effortless as possible. Its primary function is to safely guide you back to civilization. Other glampbots can assemble a tent, start small fires, calculate weather forecasts, and even synthesize food using UPBs. Glampbots use solar panels to recharge their internal batteries, allowing them to stay active as long as they get at least 6 hours of sunlight for every 24 hours they remain activated.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Glamp On!</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span> (auditory, manipulate)</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You command the glampbot to guide you back to a specific location. If you’re on a planet without GPS satellites, it can only return you to locations the glampbot has physically been before.</p>\n<p>A tactical glampbot can help build a camp, providing a +1 item bonus to Survival checks to Subsist when building a shelter. It can also synthesize an edible meal with enough sustenance for a creature for 1 day by using 1 UPB.</p><p>As tactical, but an advanced glampbot can also synthesize more complex ingredients to provide a higher-end meal equivalent to fine dining for one creature by using 5 UPB. It also helps point out threats caused by dangerous environments, granting you a +1 item bonus to Perception checks to find environmental hazards.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":6},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":2500}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"glampbot-advanced","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"glampbot"}},"_id":"38f6cbf928cd66b8"}
{"name":"Glampbot (Superior)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>The glampbot, a must-have for outdoor influencers, makes camping in the wilderness as comfortable and effortless as possible. Its primary function is to safely guide you back to civilization. Other glampbots can assemble a tent, start small fires, calculate weather forecasts, and even synthesize food using UPBs. Glampbots use solar panels to recharge their internal batteries, allowing them to stay active as long as they get at least 6 hours of sunlight for every 24 hours they remain activated.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Glamp On!</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span> (auditory, manipulate)</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You command the glampbot to guide you back to a specific location. If you’re on a planet without GPS satellites, it can only return you to locations the glampbot has physically been before.</p>\n<p>A tactical glampbot can help build a camp, providing a +1 item bonus to Survival checks to Subsist when building a shelter. It can also synthesize an edible meal with enough sustenance for a creature for 1 day by using 1 UPB.</p><p>As tactical, but an advanced glampbot can also synthesize more complex ingredients to provide a higher-end meal equivalent to fine dining for one creature by using 5 UPB. It also helps point out threats caused by dangerous environments, granting you a +1 item bonus to Perception checks to find environmental hazards.</p><p>As advanced, but the sensors of a superior glampbot are constantly scanning for suspect shifts in the environment, allowing you to attempt a check to find environmental hazards that normally require you to be Searching. You still need to meet any other requirements to find the hazard.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":10},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":10000}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"glampbot-superior","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"glampbot"}},"_id":"53e73135861cd662"}
{"name":"Grabot (Commercial)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Grabots are advertised as “your reason to never get up from the couch!” They resemble flying cylinders with a claw suspended on a retractable cable it can use to carefully pick up and drop items on command. All commercially sold grabots have at least one line in their terms of service against using the minibot for burglary, but this hasn’t stopped enterprising criminals from using them to infiltrate homes and businesses.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Grab On</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span> (auditory, manipulate)</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You command the minibot to Interact to pick up an unattended object of Light bulk or less up to 10 feet below it.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":2},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":250}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"grabot-commercial","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"grabot"}},"_id":"f45ceb1a1ab1da80"}
{"name":"Grabot (Tactical)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Grabots are advertised as “your reason to never get up from the couch!” They resemble flying cylinders with a claw suspended on a retractable cable it can use to carefully pick up and drop items on command. All commercially sold grabots have at least one line in their terms of service against using the minibot for burglary, but this hasn’t stopped enterprising criminals from using them to infiltrate homes and businesses.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Grab On</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span> (auditory, manipulate)</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You command the minibot to Interact to pick up an unattended object of Light bulk or less up to 10 feet below it.</p>\n<p>The minibot can Grab On to an object of 1 Bulk or less up to 20 feet below it.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":3},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":500}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"grabot-tactical","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"grabot"}},"_id":"755983d417c112d6"}
{"name":"Grabot (Advanced)","type":"equipment","img":"icons/commodities/tech/electronics-tech-sensor-orange-teal.webp","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"containerId":null,"description":{"value":"<p>Grabots are advertised as “your reason to never get up from the couch!” They resemble flying cylinders with a claw suspended on a retractable cable it can use to carefully pick up and drop items on command. All commercially sold grabots have at least one line in their terms of service against using the minibot for burglary, but this hasn’t stopped enterprising criminals from using them to infiltrate homes and businesses.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Grab On</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">1</span> (auditory, manipulate)</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You command the minibot to Interact to pick up an unattended object of Light bulk or less up to 10 feet below it.</p>\n<p>The minibot can Grab On to an object of 1 Bulk or less up to 20 feet below it.</p><p>The minibot can Grab On to an object of 2 Bulk or less up to 50 feet below it.</p>"},"hardness":0,"hp":{"max":0,"value":0},"level":{"value":4},"material":{"grade":null,"type":null},"price":{"value":{"sp":750}},"publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"quantity":1,"rules":[],"size":"med","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["minibot","tech"]},"usage":{"value":"held-in-one-hand"},"slug":"grabot-advanced","equipped":{"carryType":"held"}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"group":"grabot"}},"_id":"8784e0e4d3ee1fad"}
{"name":"Direct Minibot","type":"action","img":"icons/svg/target.svg","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"system":{"slug":"direct-minibot","actionType":{"value":"action"},"actions":{"value":1},"category":"interaction","publication":{"title":"Tech Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><p>You turn some dials and flick some levers to activate the linked minibot. You Activate Minibot for the linked minibot.</p><p>@Localize[SFMTP.ManualActionHint]</p>"},"rules":[],"traits":{"rarity":"common","value":["manipulate"],"otherTags":[]}},"flags":{"sf2e-missing-tech-pets":{"moduleProvided":true,"minibot":true,"itemKind":"minibot-action"}},"_id":"f34c85d67dd1e5d7"}
